		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Where do you get the data to put in the inertial tag in MuJoCo?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=43898#p43898"><![CDATA[
I don't know if this is true (never used MuJoCo) but given the nature of the other data, I suspect "pos" is the position of the center of mass in the local frame. So for a cube it would be the point in the very center of the cube, equidistant to all faces.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=748">raigan2</a> — Thu Feb 24, 2022 4:23 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
